#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:12
#: 772e49eb15794517b320de6e4086e7b9
msgid "Normal Flying-wing aircraft uses two control surfaces as Elevons to control pitch and roll. In some cases, rudders are added to the winglets to control yaw. Differential spoiler takes advantage of splitting elevons into 4 independent control surfaces: normal elevon functions are reserved for pitch and roll control, but yaw control is done by using two surfaces on one side of the wing to create drag force thus controlling yaw motion, emulating rudder control. If calibrated correctly, it will ensure pilot has smooth yaw control via rudder input during take-off and landing as well as allowing the pilot to compensate for slip/skid compensation during turning (similar to differential aileron)."
msgstr ""

