#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:63
#: 80dce9d77dd44f58b89689dda4cc681a
msgid "You can adjust the direction of each servo using the SERVOn_REVERSED parameters, and swap channels to get the right movement direction for elevons and rudder. Flap operation is also possible. The weighting of flap input to the movement of the outer and inner control surfaces can be set using :ref:`DSPOILER_CROW_W1 <DSPOILER_CROW_W1>` and :ref:`DSPOILER_CROW_W2 <DSPOILER_CROW_W2>` respectively. The default value of \"0\" for each parameter is no flap action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:68
#: b22d308713ab474c89675cd2f72728ac
msgid "manual flap control is controlled by any RC channel whose ``RCx_OPTION`` is set to \"208\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:71
#: 04e890b3449d43698a9a6edabd1e853d
msgid "Differential Spoiler options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:72
#: ff03787a9f7049eeafcdb59e2c03f32a
msgid ":ref:`DSPOILER_OPTS <DSPOILER_OPTS>` parameter gives several options that can be used to tailor the dspoiler functionality to your aircraft. They can be used to setup a 'full house' wing on a glider. :ref:`DSPOILER_OPTS<DSPOILER_OPTS>` is a bit-mask each, bit enables different functionality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:77
#: c01f0d0f15454016aac293dc21fb9e18
msgid "**Bit**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:79
#: a66fd30f8a3f4f309da1b73c3a3ee04e
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:79
#: eee9356c7b364229b425dbadef24fabc
msgid "Pitch control, this bit enables or disables pitch control output using the differential spoilers. 1 uses elevons as source for use with a flying wing, 0 uses ailerons as source for use with a traditional plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:83
#: 2e63687232dd43f5b8e6df13fbddee9c
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:83
#: 384275c89e7541349dfe26631c754a60
msgid "Full span ailerons, 1 uses both the inner and outer control surfaces for roll control 0 just used the outer control surfaces"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:86
#: 97e8c6cfc85a498caa0a532b6e595a83
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:86
#: ab1f0becd8984a21a76d7e9abfb848b8
msgid "Progressive crow, 0 gives crow brakes - the inner control surfaces are moved down and the outer surfaces moved up at the same time 1, for 0 to 50% flap only the inner surfaces are moved down then from 50% to 100% flap the outer surfaces are moved up, this gives traditional flaps first then crow brakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:92
#: e4e24c8bab0548fdb589ca3e632c3ba9
msgid "Defaults are bit 0 and bit 1 set to 1. **Conventional planes and gliders will probably want to change bit 0 to \"0\".**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:94
#: a7fa1ecc7a95444d8859ac54da0ae077
msgid ":ref:`DSPOILER_AILMTCH <DSPOILER_AILMTCH>` allows the downwards travel of the inner surfaces to be limited to a percentage of their full downwards travel. This only affects the travel when the control surfaces are used as full span ailerons or for differential yaw. Using this parameter a flap control surface with lots of downwards travel can still be utilized for full span ailerons. Upwards travel of the control surfaces is unaffected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:106
#: 5152a2a2ea484e0d98a1fd36972e65ae
msgid "Crow Mode Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:108
#: 2a83f79a879843f68775722b6393e435
msgid "If Differential Spoilers are used, setting an ``RCx_OPTION`` channel to \"87\" will allow the control of CROW aileron (outer spoilers) operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:110
#: c45f6a74fb54455f87b4061a36930fc9
msgid "HIGH position: No change to CROW deflection amount or use of progressive crow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:111
#: 5039de503f9a4bbbb86c75017ab165df
msgid "MIDDLE position: force progressive crow, assuming :ref:`DSPOILER_CROW_W1<DSPOILER_CROW_W1>` is non-zero, even if :ref:`DSPOILER_OPTS <DSPOILER_OPTS>` bit 2 is zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:112
#: 65e872a7c80543d38fe74e03d7fac0df
msgid "LOW position: effectively sets :ref:`DSPOILER_CROW_W1<DSPOILER_CROW_W1>` to zero. Only inner spoilers move with FLAP channel, ie normal flaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/differential-spoilers.rst:114
#: 6aa4df0be2624020a98009e6f859831d
msgid "This allows live changes to CROW operation on approaches so that speed braking and descent rates can be changed during the approach."
msgstr ""
